# Bench-only fragment, layered ON TOP of sdkconfig.bench. NEVER part of a release.
#
# Turns the board into a measurement source: the AirPlay receiver is not started
# and hk_tone steps through a fixed list of frequencies instead, logging each one
# before it sounds. It exists because a phone signal-generator app stopped at
# 100 Hz and the woofer's resonance is at or below that -- the one part of the
# curve that decides Fs was the part the app could not reach.
#
# THE AMPLIFIER MUST BE OUT OF THE PATH. The XH-A232 has no mute or shutdown
# input, so the bench exception in sdkconfig.bench, which releases the DAC's
# mute, releases the amplifiers with it: whatever the DAC puts out, they
# amplify. Keeping the amp out is a wiring act and cannot be a configuration
# act, which is why the sweep begins with ten seconds of silence.
#
#   idf.py -C firmware -B firmware/build-sweep \
#     -D SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.bench;sdkconfig.sweep" \
#     -D SDKCONFIG="$PWD/firmware/build-sweep/sdkconfig" build
CONFIG_HK_BENCH_TONE_INSTEAD_OF_AIRPLAY=y
CONFIG_HK_BENCH_SWEEP=y
CONFIG_HK_BENCH_SWEEP_FINE_HZ=0
